libdeflate 1.19 by Eric Biggers (MIT, see COPYING), only the files gzip compression needs.

Source: https://github.com/ebiggers/libdeflate/releases/download/v1.19/libdeflate-1.19.tar.gz
SHA-256: d9bb9bdd8cc5a8c1f7f6226fa0053dd72861e15f366e7ff7d0d191eac16d66f3

Files are copied unchanged from the tarball, at the same paths, except:
- lib/utils.c: its FREESTANDING fallback memset/memcpy/memmove/memcmp are removed. They are weak symbols, as Zig's
  compiler_rt versions are, so the linker could pick these byte-at-a-time loops for the whole server.
- lib/ht_matchfinder.h: HT_MATCHFINDER_HASH_ORDER is 11, not 15. Level 1 clears its whole hash table on every
  call; at 11 that is 8 KB instead of 128 KB, which is most of the cost of a 1-5 KB body. Output grows by 0-1%
  on captured API bodies (3% on a 54 KB list). build.sh compiles the five .c files with -DFREESTANDING
and no libc; the server passes its own malloc and free to libdeflate_alloc_compressor_ex (src/gzip.zig).
